claude-tray for Debian and Ubuntu
=================================

This package installs the extension system-wide at:

  /usr/share/gnome-shell/extensions/claude-tray@awkto.github.io

GNOME Shell extensions are enabled per user, so the package deliberately does
not change dconf settings from its root post-installation process.

If you previously installed the release zip, uninstall that per-user copy
before installing this package so it does not shadow the system copy:

  gnome-extensions uninstall claude-tray@awkto.github.io

After the first installation, log out and back in, then run as your desktop
user:

  gnome-extensions enable claude-tray@awkto.github.io

Open settings with:

  gnome-extensions prefs claude-tray@awkto.github.io

APT upgrades replace the system extension files in place. Restart the GNOME
session after an upgrade if the running shell has not picked up the new code.

ChatGPT/Codex limits require a Codex CLI installation signed in with ChatGPT.
The extension searches PATH, ~/.local/bin/codex, ~/.npm-global/bin/codex,
/usr/local/bin/codex, and /usr/bin/codex. A custom path can be set in the
extension preferences.
